      "issue": "The test 'places step_frontier_budget right after the phase_init seed step' never asserts that the budget step comes after the seed step. It slices text from the seed index to the budget index. If step_frontier_budget were moved above step_frontier_seed, that slice is the empty string, the step-key match count is 0, and the test passes. The order it names can be reversed without the test going red. It still fails when another step sits between the two, so this is a partial assertion gap (test-quality checklist, P2), not a test that cannot fail.",
      "evidence": {
        "cmd": "node -e 'const text=\"x\\n      step_frontier_budget:\\n  a: 1\\n      step_frontier_seed:\\n\"; const initSeed=text.indexOf(\"      step_frontier_seed:\\n\"); const between=text.slice(initSeed, text.indexOf(\"      step_frontier_budget:\\n\")); console.log(JSON.stringify(between), (between.match(/\\n      step_[a-z_]+:\\n/g) ?? []).length);'",
        "exit": 0,
        "out": "\"\" 0"
      },
      "fix": {
        "old": "    expect(budget.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);",
        "new": "    expect(budget.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(text.indexOf('      step_frontier_budget:\\n')).toBeGreaterThan(initSeed);"
